{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a 512 MiB file-backed LUKS2 encrypted XFS volume on node1. It automatically unlocks and mounts at /srv/secure during boot. A full node reboot confirmed persistence and recovery.","actions_performed":["Installed cryptsetup.","Generated the encryption key locally on node1 and restricted it to root with mode 0600.","Created the LUKS2 container, decrypted mapper, and XFS filesystem.","Configured automatic unlocking in /etc/crypttab and mounting in /etc/fstab.","Verified configuration-driven unlock/mount behavior before reboot.","Rebooted node1 and verified the changed boot identity, healthy system, active encryption and mount units, and persistent test data."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure","command_ids":["cmd-10eefb23b68a42b9","cmd-6b06a23503cd4a09"],"summary":"Shows valid LUKS2 metadata and the active encrypted mapper mounted as XFS at /srv/secure."},{"requirement":"Automatic unlock and mount at boot","command_ids":["cmd-7b8d508b2c754671","cmd-94477be1ad524ef7"],"summary":"Shows generated cryptsetup and mount units plus boot-journal proof that systemd unlocked and mounted the volume automatically."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-1e603a6b72a34a63","cmd-51020660bc3c4c8a","cmd-fbe999f7cdde40bd","cmd-94477be1ad524ef7"],"summary":"Captures the healthy baseline boot ID, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot ID, and recovered encrypted volume with preserved data and zero failed units."}]}
